# CR 702.16k, 702.16b, 702.16e: "You have protection from each of your opponents" - Bot1, who casts Absolute Virtue on
# turn 1 with Black Lotus and five Moxen, can't be the target of Bot2's spells (Lightning Bolt) or abilities (Fanatical
# Firebrand's), and the combat damage of Bot2's creature is prevented. The protection is the player's, not the
# creature's: Bot2's Bolt targets Absolute Virtue itself (the positive control for the spell, 3 damage marked on it), and
# on turn 4 so does Firebrand's ability. Bot1's own spell still targets Bot1 (protection is from opponents only): turn 3's
# Ancestral Recall draws three.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Absolute Virtue
Ancestral Recall
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Fanatical Firebrand
Lightning Bolt
Island x16

